{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1105994-1e-can-healing-heart-hone-another-s-form-etc-be-used-on-oneself","id":1105994,"title":"1e: Can Healing Heart, Hone Another's Form, etc, be used on oneself?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-21T03:27:16-07:00","id":1105994,"title":"1e: Can Healing Heart, Hone Another's Form, etc, be used on oneself?","content":"A lot of the self-only spells have an identical version for one dot more that can be used on others. My question is, do these advanced version of the spells HAVE to be used on others? I know it doesn't really matter when it comes to spontaneous casting, but if, for example, I knew Healing Heart as a rote but did not know Self-Healing as a rote, could I cast the Healing Heart rote on myself? Same question for any of the other similar spells. There is an obvious advantage there for rote casting, and even more so for Proximi that know one as a blessing but not another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12390-gadren","name":"gadren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T03:44:53-07:00","id":1105996,"title":"","content":"You can always target yourself with your spells.<br /> <br /> If I recall correctly Healing Heart is a dot higher than Self-Healing because in 1e viable spell targets worked by dot level, at the most basic you could cast it on yourself, then a dot more you could cast it on another, then a dot after that you could cast it at sensory range. Being a higher level dot means the spells is exactly the same, it's just expanded the parameters for what counts as a viable target.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 06-21-2017, 06:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T10:23:04-07:00","id":1106125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1105994-1e-can-healing-heart-hone-another-s-form-etc-be-used-on-oneself?p=1105996#post1105996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can always target yourself with your spells.</div> </div> </div> </div> Is there a rules citation for that? (For the record, I think it SHOULD work that way, but want to find any rules on the matter.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1105994-1e-can-healing-heart-hone-another-s-form-etc-be-used-on-oneself?p=1105996#post1105996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I recall correctly Healing Heart is a dot higher than Self-Healing because in 1e viable spell targets worked by dot level, at the most basic you could cast it on yourself, then a dot more you could cast it on another, then a dot after that you could cast it at sensory range. Being a higher level dot means the spells is exactly the same, it's just expanded the parameters for what counts as a viable target.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, at the start of the spells section it gives a breakdown of what spells can do at different dots of arcanum (1st dot spells allow unveiling-type magic on self, 2 dot spells allow you to grant unveiling magic to others, or grant veiling or shielding magic to yourself, 3 dot spells allow you to grant veiling or shielding magic to others, etc), but the start of that states that the intention of that section is to assist with the casting of spontaneous spells. Since rotes are specific spells you have practiced casting a specific way, I could also see the argument that a rote designed to be cast on other people can't be cast on oneself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12390-gadren","name":"gadren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T15:06:31-07:00","id":1106275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;&gt; <span style=\"color:#231F20\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy-Bold\"><b>Target: </b><span style=\"color:#231F20\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\">The subject of a <span style=\"color:#231F20\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy-Italic\"><i>spell</i><span style=\"color:#231F20\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\">; the person, place or thing suffering or receiving the spell\u2019s<br /> <span style=\"color:#231F20\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy-Italic\"><i>effect</i><span style=\"color:#231F20\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\">.</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>Why would you think you cant cast a spell on yourself? You can cast any spell on yourself even damage spells. I dont think you will find text saying it any other way, the only thing you might find is specific text that says you cant cast a spell on yourself as a exception but i cant remember ever seeing an example of that either.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T15:10:21-07:00","id":1106278,"title":"","content":"Because Healing Heart and Self-healing are two different Rotes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T15:21:44-07:00","id":1106284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1105994-1e-can-healing-heart-hone-another-s-form-etc-be-used-on-oneself?p=1106275#post1106275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why would you think you cant cast a spell on yourself? You can cast any spell on yourself even damage spells. I dont think you will find text saying it any other way, the only thing you might find is specific text that says you cant cast a spell on yourself as a exception but i cant remember ever seeing an example of that either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because Healing Heart says it &quot;can heal the wounds of other humans.&quot; It does not say it can be used to heal yourself like Self-Healing does.<br /> <br /> Here is the spell text from the book for Self-Healing and Healing Heart:<br /> <br /> Self-Healing (Life \u2022\u2022)<br /> The mage can heal herself of injuries<br /> and wounds.<br /> Practice: Ruling<br /> Action: Instant<br /> Duration: Lasting<br /> Aspect: Covert<br /> Cost: 1 Mana<br /> Each success heals one point of bashing or lethal Health damage (the rightmost wound on the Health chart is healed first). This spell can be cast covertly, although Sleepers who witness it need some method of explaining its miraculous effects so the spell won\u2019t seem Improbable; use of medical gear might be enough to convince them.<br /> With Life 3, the mage can heal aggravated wounds, but the spell must be cast with a vulgar aspect.<br /> <br /> Healing Heart (Life \u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> The mage can heal the wounds of other humans.<br /> Practice: Perfecting<br /> Action: Instant<br /> Duration: Lasting<br /> Aspect: Covert<br /> Cost: 1 Mana<br /> Each success heals one bashing or lethal Health wound (the rightmost wound on the Health chart is healed first). At this level, the mage must touch the target. With Life 4, he can cast this<br /> spell at sensory range. With Life 4, aggravated wounds can be healed, although the mage must still touch the target (he can heal aggravated wounds at sensory range with Life 5).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12390-gadren","name":"gadren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T15:27:32-07:00","id":1106288,"title":"","content":"I recognize that they're two different rotes, but it seems ridiculous to me to say that the upgraded version of the spell is only good for healing other people. Easily solved though, &quot;find&quot; a rote that lets you cast healing effects on yourself or others at your leisure, still just Life 3.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T15:35:08-07:00","id":1106293,"title":"","content":"Yes this is just because 1e required +1 arcanum to affect other peeps. Its odd, technically if you have life 3 and are healing yourself you will use self-healing cos you can remove agg, but theres no reason why you couldnt use healing heart on yourself (it just requires touch which you can do to youself easily) but why would you unless you only have healing heart as a rote maybe?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T17:10:02-07:00","id":1106331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1105994-1e-can-healing-heart-hone-another-s-form-etc-be-used-on-oneself?p=1106293#post1106293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...but why would you unless you only have healing heart as a rote maybe?</div> </div> </div> </div> correct, that is the crux of the question. A mage that learned Healing Heart as a rote but not Self-Healing would get more successes and risk less paradox with that rote than spontaneously casting Self-Healing on himself. Likewise, a Proximi may have learned the Healing Heart rote as a blessing but not Self Healing, and doesn't have the option to cast spontaneously.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12390-gadren","name":"gadren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T12:09:29-07:00","id":1106676,"title":"","content":"My advice - Get 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T20:50:12-07:00","id":1106858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1105994-1e-can-healing-heart-hone-another-s-form-etc-be-used-on-oneself?p=1106676#post1106676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My advice - Get 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>I own it, but the group prefers 1e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12390-gadren","name":"gadren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}